export const PRIVACY_POLICY_MARKDOWN: string = "# **Repeto Privacy Policy**\n\n**Effective Date:** September 2026  \n**Last Updated:** September 2026\n\nRepeto (“Repeto,” “we,” “our,” or “us”) respects your privacy and is committed to handling your information responsibly. This Privacy Policy explains how information is collected, used, stored, shared, and protected when you use the Repeto mobile application and related services (collectively, the “Service”).\n\nBy continuing to use Repeto, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.\n\n---\n\n## **1\\. About Repeto**\n\nRepeto is a productivity and personal organization application designed to help individuals, roommates, couples, families, and other groups organize recurring responsibilities and household activities.\n\nThe Service may include features such as:\n\n* Personal and shared task management;  \n* Recurring routines and schedules;  \n* Reminders and alarms;  \n* Bill and expense reminders;  \n* Medicine and health-related reminders;  \n* Household and chore coordination;  \n* Multiple household spaces;  \n* Task assignments and chore rotation;  \n* Household activity and accountability features;  \n* Streaks and completion tracking;  \n* Push notifications and device alarms;  \n* QR-code-based household invitations;  \n* Offline access and synchronization;  \n* In-app customer support;  \n* Bilingual English and Hindi functionality; and  \n* Calendar export functionality.\n\nFeatures may be added, modified, or removed as Repeto upgrades.\n\n---\n\n## **2\\. Eligibility and Children’s Privacy**\n\nRepeto is intended for individuals who are **12 years of age or older**.\n\nBy creating or using a Repeto account, you confirm that:\n\n1. You are at least 12 years old; and  \n2. The information you provide is accurate to the best of your knowledge.\n\nRepeto is not intentionally designed to collect personal information from children under 12\\.\n\nIf we become aware that personal information has been collected from a child under 12 without appropriate authorization, we will take reasonable steps to review and delete that information where required by applicable law.\n\nParents or guardians who believe that a child may have provided personal information to Repeto may contact us using the support information provided in this Privacy Policy.\n\n---\n\n# **3\\. Information We Collect**\n\nThe information collected by Repeto depends on the features you use and the information you choose to provide.\n\n## **3.1 Account and Authentication Information**\n\nWhen you create or access a Repeto account, we may collect or receive:\n\n* Google display name;  \n* Email address;  \n* Profile photograph or profile image URL;  \n* Firebase user identifier (UID);  \n* Authentication and session information;  \n* Account creation information;  \n* Account activity information; and  \n* Information associated with your authentication method.\n\nRepeto supports Google Sign-In and may use Firebase Authentication to authenticate users and manage secure account sessions.\n\nWhen using email-based authentication or account-related authentication emails, automated emails may be sent from:\n\n**noreply.repeto@gmail.com**\n\nThis address is used for automated login or authentication-related communication and is not intended to function as a customer-support inbox.\n\nWhen you use Google Sign-In, certain account information may be provided to Repeto by Google according to your Google account settings and applicable Google policies.\n\n---\n\n## **3.2 Terms and Consent Information**\n\nWhen you first access Repeto, the application requires acknowledgment of the Terms of Service and Privacy Policy before account access can proceed.\n\nRepeto records the date and time associated with this acknowledgment, including a `termsAcceptedAt` timestamp, for account and compliance purposes.\n\n---\n\n## **3.3 Phone Number**\n\nRepeto may request a mobile phone number during profile setup.\n\nThe phone number may be used for purposes including:\n\n* Household member identification;  \n* Helping household members recognize one another;  \n* Household coordination;  \n* Chore identification; and  \n* Account profile information.\n\nThe phone number is user-provided profile information and does not by itself indicate that the number has been independently verified through an SMS one-time-password process.\n\nYou should provide only a phone number that you are authorized to use.\n\n---\n\n## **3.4 Personal Tasks, Routines, and Schedules**\n\nWhen you create tasks or routines, Repeto may collect information such as:\n\n* Task titles;  \n* Task descriptions;  \n* Notes;  \n* Categories;  \n* Recurrence rules;  \n* Reminder times;  \n* Due dates;  \n* Completion status;  \n* Skip and snooze information;  \n* Completion history;  \n* Streak information;  \n* Assigned users;  \n* Archived tasks;  \n* Pinned tasks;  \n* Task creation and modification information; and  \n* Other information that you voluntarily enter into the Service.\n\nRepeto may interpret information entered through its task creation interface to identify details such as amounts, categories, recurrence patterns, dates, and reminder times.\n\n---\n\n## **3.5 Financial and Bill Information**\n\nRepeto allows users to organize bills, expenses, and other financial reminders.\n\nThis may include:\n\n* Bill names;  \n* Expense descriptions;  \n* Monetary amounts;  \n* Payment due dates;  \n* Recurring payment schedules;  \n* Financial categories; and  \n* Related notes or task information.\n\nFor example, a user may create a reminder such as “Rent ₹15,000 every month.”\n\nRepeto is **not a bank, payment processor, payment gateway, wallet, or financial institution**.\n\nRepeto does not process monetary transactions through the Service and does not require users to provide bank passwords, UPI PINs, card numbers, or banking credentials for ordinary bill and expense organization.\n\nRepeto processes financial information entered by users for organizational and reminder purposes.\n\nUsers should avoid entering unnecessary confidential financial information into the Service.\n\nFinancial summaries, calculations, forecasts, or insights provided by Repeto are intended for organizational purposes and should be reviewed by the user before being relied upon for financial decisions.\n\n---\n\n## **3.6 Medicine and Health-Related Information**\n\nRepeto may allow users to create medicine-related routines and reminders.\n\nDepending on what you enter, this information may include:\n\n* Medicine names;  \n* Dosage information;  \n* Medication schedules;  \n* Multiple daily doses;  \n* Refill reminders;  \n* Health-related notes; and  \n* Other information voluntarily entered into medicine-related tasks.\n\nThis information may be sensitive personal information.\n\nRepeto is designed as a **self-management and organizational reminder tool**. It is not a medical professional, healthcare provider, diagnostic service, emergency medical service, or substitute for professional medical advice.\n\nRepeto does not diagnose medical conditions or provide medical treatment recommendations.\n\nUsers remain responsible for reviewing their medication schedules and following instructions provided by their healthcare professionals.\n\n---\n\n## **3.7 Household Information**\n\nRepeto allows users to create and participate in multiple household spaces.\n\nA user may create or join up to five household spaces, depending on the features available in the application.\n\nHousehold information may include:\n\n* Household name;  \n* Household emoji or identifier;  \n* Household membership;  \n* Member identifiers;  \n* Assigned tasks;  \n* Shared task information;  \n* Completion activity;  \n* Chore rotation information;  \n* Household activity;  \n* Member-related task statistics; and  \n* Other information associated with household collaboration.\n\n---\n\n## **3.8 Household Codes and QR Information**\n\nRepeto may provide a permanent personal code for household invitations and member discovery.\n\nUsers may join households through:\n\n* Entering another user's Repeto code; or  \n* Scanning an in-app household or member QR code.\n\nThe QR scanning feature is used to process the QR information necessary to establish the intended household connection.\n\n---\n\n## **3.9 Support Tickets and Support Communications**\n\nRepeto provides an in-app support system.\n\nWhen you submit a support request, we may collect:\n\n* Support ticket subject;  \n* Message content;  \n* Priority selected by you;  \n* Your account information;  \n* Associated email address;  \n* Support responses;  \n* Ticket status; and  \n* Information necessary to resolve the support request.\n\nSupport tickets may be stored in Repeto's cloud infrastructure and may remain available for customer-service and support-audit purposes.\n\n---\n\n## **3.10 Device and Technical Information**\n\nRepeto may collect or maintain limited technical and operational information necessary to provide and maintain the Service, including:\n\n* Device platform;  \n* Application version;  \n* Operating system version;  \n* Last active timestamp;  \n* Push-notification information;  \n* Synchronization information;  \n* Account activity information; and  \n* Other technical information required for feature compatibility and service operation.\n\nCertain session-related information may be periodically updated so that the latest relevant device or application information is available.\n\n---\n\n# **4\\. Camera and QR-Code Scanning**\n\nRepeto requests camera access exclusively for QR-code scanning functionality.\n\nWhen you use the QR scanner:\n\n* Camera frames are analyzed in real time;  \n* QR information is processed for the selected scanning operation;  \n* Camera footage is not intentionally recorded;  \n* Camera photographs are not intentionally saved; and  \n* The camera feed is not uploaded as a video or photo to Repeto servers.\n\nThe camera feed used for QR scanning is processed in device memory during the scanning operation and is intended to have **zero retention as camera footage**.\n\nCamera permission is not required for ordinary task management.\n\n---\n\n# **5\\. Device Permissions**\n\nRepeto may request Android permissions necessary for specific application functionality.\n\n### **Notifications**\n\nThe notification permission allows Repeto to send relevant reminders, task alerts, household updates, nudges, and other notifications selected or generated through the Service.\n\n### **Exact Alarms**\n\nRepeto may request exact-alarm permission to schedule time-specific alarms for recurring responsibilities.\n\n### **Full-Screen Alarm Display**\n\nRepeto may use Android full-screen notification functionality for alarm experiences that are designed to appear prominently when an alarm is triggered.\n\n### **Wake Lock**\n\nRepeto may use a wake lock when an alarm is triggered to allow the device to remain active briefly while the alarm experience is presented.\n\n### **Vibration**\n\nVibration permission may be used for alarm and notification feedback.\n\n### **Device Restart**\n\nRepeto may use Android's boot-completion functionality to restore or reschedule applicable pending alarms after a device restart.\n\nYou can manage available permissions through your Android device settings. Disabling certain permissions may affect the corresponding Repeto features.\n\n---\n\n### **6\\. Reminders, Notifications, and Alarm Functionality**\n\nRepeto is designed to help users manage recurring responsibilities through scheduled notifications and device alarms.\n\nDepending on the task and device configuration, Repeto may use:\n\n* Standard push notifications;  \n* Local notifications;  \n* Exact Android alarms;  \n* Full-screen alarm interfaces;  \n* Sound and vibration;  \n* Household notifications;  \n* Task completion notifications; and  \n* Household member nudges.\n\nRepeto makes reasonable efforts to schedule and provide reminders according to the configurations selected by users.\n\nReminder and alarm behavior may depend on the device, operating system, application state, connectivity, and other technical conditions. This may include notification permissions, exact-alarm permissions, battery-management settings, background restrictions, device restarts, device date and time, time-zone settings, travel between different time zones, changes to system time settings, synchronization status, push-notification infrastructure, or other circumstances affecting the operation of the device or Service.\n\nIn some circumstances, temporary technical conditions, synchronization delays, device restrictions, or other unforeseen conditions may affect the timing, display, synchronization, or receipt of a reminder or notification.\n\nRepeto is designed to work with the device and system capabilities available to it. Users are encouraged to keep their device date, time, and time-zone settings accurate and to maintain the permissions required for the reminder features they use.\n\nFor responsibilities involving health, safety, payments, legal deadlines, or other significant consequences, users should maintain appropriate alternative arrangements.\n\n---\n\n# **7\\. Household Collaboration and Shared Information**\n\nRepeto is designed to support shared household organization.\n\nWhen you join or participate in a household, information associated with that shared household may be accessible to other authorized household members.\n\nDepending on the feature, household members may be able to see:\n\n* Shared tasks;  \n* Task titles and descriptions;  \n* Notes associated with shared tasks;  \n* Due dates;  \n* Recurring schedules;  \n* Assigned members;  \n* Completion information;  \n* Chore rotation activity;  \n* Household activity;  \n* Relevant accountability statistics; and  \n* Other information intentionally placed within the shared household workspace.\n\n### **Household Visibility**\n\nInformation added to a shared household should be considered information that may be accessible to other authorized members of that household.\n\nRepeto's shared household functionality does **not currently provide separate field-level privacy filters or category-level privacy controls** that allow individual fields within an otherwise shared task to be hidden from household members.\n\nIf you want information to remain personal, you should keep it within your personal task space rather than adding it to a shared household.\n\nYou are responsible for reviewing household membership and considering the information you choose to share.\n\n---\n\n# **8\\. Household Activity, Nudges, and Accountability Features**\n\nRepeto may provide features intended to assist household coordination, including:\n\n* Task assignment;  \n* Rotating chores;  \n* Completion updates;  \n* Overdue-task nudges;  \n* Household activity notifications;  \n* Completion percentages;  \n* Streaks;  \n* Best streaks;  \n* Total completed repetitions; and  \n* Household accountability leaderboards.\n\nThese features are based on activity recorded within the Service.\n\nFor example, completion information may be used to calculate whether a task was completed on time, late, missed, or skipped.\n\nHousehold members may therefore see certain activity or statistics associated with shared tasks.\n\n---\n\n# **9\\. Offline Storage and Synchronization**\n\nRepeto is designed to support offline use.\n\nWhen the device is offline, task and routine changes may be stored locally using the application's local storage systems.\n\nRepeto may use:\n\n* Native SQLite storage; and  \n* Android application storage mechanisms such as AsyncStorage.\n\nWhen internet connectivity becomes available, pending changes may be synchronized with Repeto's cloud infrastructure.\n\nOffline synchronization may involve a local queue of pending changes.\n\nThe information displayed while offline may not immediately reflect changes made from another device or by another household member until synchronization occurs.\n\n---\n\n# **10\\. How We Use Information**\n\nRepeto may use collected information to:\n\n* Create and manage accounts;  \n* Authenticate users;  \n* Provide personal tasks and routines;  \n* Schedule reminders and alarms;  \n* Synchronize information between devices and cloud services;  \n* Support offline functionality;  \n* Coordinate household activities;  \n* Assign and rotate chores;  \n* Deliver household nudges and notifications;  \n* Maintain completion history and streaks;  \n* Calculate household accountability statistics;  \n* Provide bill and expense organization;  \n* Provide medicine and health-related reminders;  \n* Provide support services;  \n* Process QR-code invitations;  \n* Provide calendar export functionality;  \n* Maintain application security;  \n* Improve application functionality and compatibility;  \n* Diagnose operational or compatibility issues;  \n* Respond to support requests;  \n* Prevent misuse or unauthorized activity; and  \n* Comply with applicable legal obligations.\n\nWe use information for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy and for purposes reasonably connected with providing the Service.\n\n---\n\n# **11\\. Data Storage**\n\nRepeto uses Google Firebase services and local device storage to provide the Service.\n\nDepending on the type of information, data may be stored in:\n\n* Firebase Authentication;  \n* Google Cloud Firestore;  \n* Firebase Cloud Functions-related infrastructure;  \n* Local SQLite storage; and  \n* Local application storage.\n\nTask information may be stored within personal or household-related cloud collections depending on whether the task is personal or shared.\n\nSupport tickets may be stored within Repeto's support infrastructure.\n\n---\n\n# **12\\. Third-Party Services**\n\nRepeto uses third-party technology and infrastructure providers to operate certain parts of the Service.\n\nThese may include:\n\n### **Google Firebase**\n\nRepeto uses Firebase services for authentication, cloud database functionality, synchronization, and related application infrastructure.\n\n### **Google Sign-In**\n\nGoogle Sign-In may be used to authenticate Repeto accounts.\n\n### **Google Cloud Firestore**\n\nFirestore is used to store and synchronize cloud-based Repeto information.\n\n### **Firebase Cloud Functions**\n\nCloud Functions may be used to perform server-side application logic and automated service operations.\n\n### **Expo / Expo Application Services**\n\nRepeto uses Expo technologies and related application services as part of its application infrastructure, including application build and update functionality.\n\n### **Firebase Cloud Messaging**\n\nPush notifications on supported Android devices may involve Firebase Cloud Messaging infrastructure.\n\nThese third-party services may process information according to their respective terms, privacy policies, and security practices.\n\nRepeto does not control the independent privacy practices of third-party providers.\n\n---\n\n# **13\\. Data Sharing**\n\n## **13.1 Household Members**\n\nInformation intentionally placed in a shared household may be accessible to authorized members of that household.\n\n## **13.2 Service Providers**\n\nInformation may be processed by technology providers that help Repeto provide authentication, cloud storage, synchronization, notifications, application infrastructure, and other necessary technical services.\n\n## **13.3 Legal Requirements**\n\nRepeto may disclose information where reasonably necessary to:\n\n* Comply with applicable law;  \n* Respond to valid legal processes;  \n* Protect the security or rights of users or others;  \n* Investigate fraud or misuse;  \n* Prevent security incidents; or  \n* Enforce applicable agreements or policies.\n\n## **13.4 Business Transactions**\n\nIf Repeto or substantially all of its assets becomes involved in a merger, acquisition, restructuring, financing, sale, or similar transaction, information may be transferred as part of that transaction subject to applicable law.\n\n---\n\n## **14\\. Use and Disclosure of Personal Information**\n\nRepeto uses personal information to provide, maintain, secure, and improve the Service and to support the features and functionality described in this Privacy Policy.\n\nInformation may be processed or disclosed to service providers, technology providers, business partners, or other parties where reasonably necessary to operate, maintain, improve, secure, or provide the Service, subject to applicable law and the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.\n\nRepeto does not disclose personal information except as described in this Privacy Policy, with your direction or consent where applicable, or where permitted or required by law.\n\nWe do not sell or provide personal information to third parties in circumstances prohibited by applicable law.\n\n---\n\n# **15\\. Data Security**\n\nRepeto uses reasonable technical and organizational measures intended to protect information against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.\n\nSecurity measures may include:\n\n* Authenticated account access;  \n* Firebase authentication controls;  \n* Cloud access controls;  \n* Secure data transmission where supported;  \n* Restricted access to application infrastructure;  \n* Local application storage controls; and  \n* Reasonable operational safeguards.\n\nYou are also responsible for protecting access to your device and account.\n\nNo electronic system or internet-based service can eliminate every possible security risk. Repeto therefore uses reasonable safeguards while recognizing the technical nature of modern internet and mobile services.\n\n---\n\n# **16\\. Data Retention**\n\nRepeto retains information for as long as reasonably necessary to provide the Service, maintain account functionality, support household collaboration, provide customer support, comply with applicable obligations, maintain security, and perform other legitimate operational purposes.\n\nDifferent categories of information may have different retention periods.\n\nExamples include:\n\n* Account information: retained until account deletion according to the applicable deletion process;  \n* Personal tasks: retained while associated with the account unless deleted earlier;  \n* Deleted tasks: removed according to the applicable deletion functionality;  \n* Household information: retained while necessary for household functionality and unlinked as applicable when members leave;  \n* Device/session information: periodically updated as newer information becomes available; and  \n* Support tickets: may be retained for customer-support and support-audit purposes.\n\nLocal information may remain on a device until removed by the application, deleted by the user, or otherwise cleared from device storage.\n\n---\n\n# **17\\. Account Deletion and Data Rights**\n\nRepeto provides account-deletion functionality directly within the application.\n\nThe account deletion option is available through:\n\n**Profile → Account Actions → Delete Account**\n\nRepeto provides two deletion pathways.\n\n## **17.1 Deactivate Account — 30-Day Recovery Period**\n\nWhen a user selects the standard account-deletion option, the account may enter a **30-day recovery period**.\n\nDuring this period:\n\n* The account is marked for deletion;  \n* Access may be restricted according to the deletion state;  \n* The user may log back in to recover the account; and  \n* Previously associated routines and household memberships may be restored.\n\nIf the user restores the account within the applicable recovery period, the deletion state may be cleared and the account returned to active status.\n\n## **17.2 Start Fresh — Immediate Permanent Wipe**\n\nRepeto also provides a **Start Fresh / Permanent Wipe** option.\n\nWhen this option is selected, Repeto is designed to permanently remove the applicable account information and associated user data without waiting for the 30-day recovery period.\n\nThis may include:\n\n* Personal tasks;  \n* Routines;  \n* Reminders;  \n* Cloud profile information;  \n* Notification-related information;  \n* Local SQLite information; and  \n* Other account-associated information covered by the deletion process.\n\nThe permanent wipe is intended to be irreversible.\n\nUsers should use this option only when they are certain they no longer want the associated account information and routines.\n\n---\n\n# **18\\. Information Shared Through Households After Account Deletion**\n\nInformation that has been shared with another household member may have been viewed, copied, recorded, or otherwise retained independently by that person.\n\nDeleting your Repeto account does not control information that another user may have independently retained outside Repeto.\n\nHousehold information may also be subject to the deletion or membership rules applicable to the shared household.\n\n---\n\n# **19\\. Calendar Export**\n\nRepeto may provide an option to export routines or tasks in standard `.ics` calendar format.\n\nWhen you choose to export information, the resulting calendar file is provided for your use.\n\nOnce exported, the file may be stored or processed by your device, calendar application, cloud-storage provider, or other service selected by you.\n\nRepeto does not control how information is handled after you independently export and transfer it to another service.\n\n---\n\n# **20\\. Your Choices and Rights**\n\nDepending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights relating to your personal information, including the ability to:\n\n* Access information associated with your account;  \n* Correct inaccurate information;  \n* Delete your account and associated information;  \n* Request information about how your data is used;  \n* Manage notification permissions;  \n* Manage device permissions;  \n* Leave shared households;  \n* Delete personal tasks;  \n* Manage information shared within households; and  \n* Contact us regarding privacy concerns.\n\nYou may also use the account controls available within Repeto to manage your account and information.\n\nWe may need to verify your identity before processing certain privacy-related requests.\n\n---\n\n# **21\\. User Responsibility for Shared Content**\n\nRepeto allows users to create and share task titles, notes, descriptions, and other content within household spaces.\n\nUsers are responsible for the information and content they choose to enter or share.\n\nUsers should not use shared household features to intentionally post content that is:\n\n* Illegal;  \n* Threatening;  \n* Abusive;  \n* Harassing;  \n* Defamatory; or  \n* Otherwise inappropriate for the intended household environment.\n\nRepeto may take reasonable action regarding misuse of the Service where appropriate.\n\n---\n\n# **22\\. Information Accuracy and User Review**\n\nRepeto processes information based largely on information entered or configured by users.\n\nYou are responsible for reviewing information you enter into the Service, including:\n\n* Task names;  \n* Dates;  \n* Recurrence schedules;  \n* Reminder times;  \n* Medication schedules;  \n* Financial amounts;  \n* Household assignments; and  \n* Other user-configured information.\n\nRepeto may calculate schedules, completion statistics, streaks, percentages, summaries, or other organizational information from user-provided data.\n\nThese features are intended to assist organization and should be reviewed by the user before being relied upon for important responsibilities or decisions.\n\n---\n\n# **23\\. Reminder and Alarm Conditions**\n\nRepeto is designed to provide reminders using both application notifications and Android device alarm capabilities.\n\nDepending on the feature and device, alarm behavior may be affected by:\n\n* Android system settings;  \n* Permission settings;  \n* Battery optimization;  \n* Device manufacturer restrictions;  \n* Device date and time;  \n* Time-zone changes;  \n* Application updates;  \n* Device restart;  \n* Notification settings;  \n* Connectivity;  \n* Push-notification infrastructure; and  \n* Other operating-system or device conditions.\n\nRepeto may automatically reschedule applicable alarms after a device restart.\n\nUsers should keep the application and device operating system reasonably up to date and ensure that required permissions remain enabled for the features they wish to use.\n\nFor responsibilities where timing has significant health, safety, financial, legal, or other consequences, users should use appropriate additional safeguards.\n\n---\n\n# **24\\. Changes to This Privacy Policy**\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect:\n\n* Changes to Repeto;  \n* New features;  \n* Changes in technology;  \n* Changes in legal requirements;  \n* Changes in our data practices; or  \n* Improvements to clarity and transparency.\n\nWhen we update this Privacy Policy, we will update the “Last Updated” date shown at the beginning of the policy.\n\nWhere required by applicable law, we may provide additional notice or request consent for material changes.\n\nYour continued use of Repeto after an updated Privacy Policy becomes effective constitutes acknowledgment of the updated policy to the extent permitted by applicable law.\n\n---\n\n# **25\\. Contact Us**\n\nIf you have questions, concerns, privacy requests, account-related questions, or support requests regarding Repeto, please contact us at:\n\n**App Name:** Repeto  \n**Privacy and Support Email:** support.repeto@gmail.com  \n**Login and Authentication Email:** noreply.repeto@gmail.com  \n**Country:** India\n\nFor customer support, privacy questions, account assistance, or data-related requests:\n\n**support.repeto@gmail.com**\n\nThe address **noreply.repeto@gmail.com** is used for automated login and authentication-related emails and is not intended to function as a customer-support inbox.\n\n---\n\n# **26\\. Applicable Rights**\n\nNothing in this Privacy Policy is intended to remove, restrict, or exclude any rights or protections that cannot lawfully be excluded under applicable law.\n\nIf any provision of this Privacy Policy is determined to be invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions will continue to apply to the extent permitted by law.\n\n---\n\n**End of Privacy Policy**\n\n";
